<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Movie on Typophile Archive</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/movie/</link><description>Recent content in Movie on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 29 Jan 2015 11:59:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/movie/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Out Now: Lichtspielhaus Slab</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/122926/</link><pubDate>Thu, 29 Jan 2015 11:59:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/122926/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110840im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/highnoon-poster.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lichtspielhaus Slab is an ultra condensed typeface based on Lichtspielhaus. It still transports you back to a time where neon lights and marquee letters decorated cinema facades. This time with Slab.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110840/http:/www.myfonts.com/fonts/typocalypse/lichtspielhaus-slab/"&gt;You can get it at myfonts if you like it&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110840im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/1.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110840im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/2.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110840im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/3.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110840im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/4.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110840im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/5.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110840im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/6.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110840im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/7.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110840im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/8.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110840im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/9.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are 8 styles: Hairline, Thin, Light, Regular, Medium, Bold, Black and Heavy.&lt;br&gt;
“Lichtspielhaus Slab” is the third part of a Type Noir Quadrilogy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110840/http:/www.myfonts.com/fonts/typocalypse/lichtspielhaus-slab/"&gt;[€73,99 ↘ €14,80] Until March 16, 2015 at Myfonts &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Font used in the french movie 'Carambolages'</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/104082/</link><pubDate>Mon, 24 Jun 2013 09:57:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/104082/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Hi everyone,&lt;/p&gt;
